i=(x^2-y^2)/2$, and a stream function is $\\psi=xy$. Equipotentials satisfy $x^2-y^2=2c$; streamlines satisfy $xy=k$. Draw at least two curves of each family. Their regular intersections are orthogonal; the origin is a stagnation point.\n\n**Authored reference sketch:**\n\n![Equipotentials and streamlines for part a](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fauthored-curves-1a.png)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719458}] [:answer/id #uuid "6b8da09c-3144-58f9-a42b-54e2421ef65f" {:answer/id #uuid "6b8da09c-3144-58f9-a42b-54e2421ef65f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The counterclockwise orientation traverses the right edge upward from $(b,0)$ to $(b,1)$. Parametrize it by $\\mathbf r(t)=(b,t)$, $0\\le t\\le1$. Then\n\n$$\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=\\int_0^1(0,f(b))\\cdot(0,1)\\,dt=f(b).$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719459}] [:answer/id #uuid "7d6d5af5-6fe8-5cff-8cde-744cf4bca8cb" {:answer/id #uuid "7d6d5af5-6fe8-5cff-8cde-744cf4bca8cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{45\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719466}] [:answer/id #uuid "7f5f4c85-8d0a-5cbf-ad66-eb65561b455e" {:answer/id #uuid "7f5f4c85-8d0a-5cbf-ad66-eb65561b455e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Under Green's usual regularity hypotheses, for example if $f\\in C^1([a,b])$, the boundary calculation from (b–d) gives\n\n$$f(b)-f(a)=\\oint_{\\partial R}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=\\iint_R f'(x)\\,dA=\\int_a^b\\int_0^1f'(x)\\,dy\\,dx=\\int_a^b f'(x)\\,dx.$$\n\nThis is the **Fundamental Theorem of Calculus**, in its Newton–Leibniz form.\n\nThe source assumes only that $f$ is differentiable. That alone does not ensure continuous first partial derivatives, as required by the standard version of Green's theorem used here; the formal derivation needs the additional regularity condition above (or an appropriate generalized theorem)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719467}] [:multistep/id #uuid "8fa50f74-ea14-57c5-9cc7-9684c0dbd2ba" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719472 :multistep/context "Source: Problem 2(a–b), PDF page 3." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719454} :multistep/id #uuid "8fa50f74-ea14-57c5-9cc7-9684c0dbd2ba" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719454 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719431} :step/id #uuid "5d71f7bf-a32a-5963-b9cf-8fe1b0183278" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719473}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719473 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719457} :step/id #uuid "90ad2215-657b-5437-a146-71e22f69b2e8"}]}] [:multistep/id #uuid "a317f78d-2e52-59e3-a1f6-c0539bed7e46" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719478 :multistep/context "Source: Problem 5(a–b), PDF page 6.\n\nConsider the cardioid\n\n$$\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle\\cos t(1-\\sin t),\\ \\sin t(1-\\sin t)\\rangle,\\qquad0\\le t\\le2\\pi.$$\n\n![Source cardioid r=1-sin(t)](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fcardioid-5.png)" :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719486} :multistep/id #uuid "a317f78d-2e52-59e3-a1f6-c0539bed7e46" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719452 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719497} :step/id #uuid "50086270-5023-523d-8aa7-8ec755f23fe9"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719486 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719490} :step/id #uuid "c396a9eb-d20d-5351-9e9a-e6c0ececb5a3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719452}}]}] [:multistep/id #uuid "e5b2bfad-c83c-57c1-8b1b-52629c2657a6" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719500 :multistep/context "Source: Problem 3(a–b), PDF page 4." :multistep/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719485} :multistep/id #uuid "e5b2bfad-c83c-57c1-8b1b-52629c2657a6" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719474 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719442} :step/id #uuid "92016bbe-4ac0-5e57-960f-b29a64fb7a2c"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719485 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719498} :step/id #uuid "be1e5339-cb99-5543-95cf-22e44f3548af" :step